[17592186444651 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129525" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444651 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444651 #edb/ref 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=100$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=200.$ Find $\\text{Var}[0.5X+0.4Y].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444651 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4592eee9-4d66-541e-b103-0104f487a3d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444651 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[0.5X+0.4Y]={0.5}^{2}\\cdot 100+{0.4}^{2}\\cdot 200=57.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444652 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444652 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129526" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444652 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444652 #edb/ref 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=20$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=5.$ Find $\\text{Var}[0.5X-2Y].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444652 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4ebe566e-595e-53c5-acba-b32f38c7b929" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444652 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[0.5X-2Y]={(0.5)}^{2}\\cdot 20+{(-2)}^{2}\\cdot 5=25.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444653 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444653 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129524" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444653 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444653 #edb/ref 1071 "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\te